From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] meson: do not run the SpiderMonkey sanity check when cross compiling

meson's cxx.run() refuses to work in a cross environment that has no
exe_wrapper, and it says so by raising, before returning a result:

  meson.build:258:22: ERROR: Can not run test applications in this cross
  environment.

Buildroot's cross file sets needs_exe_wrapper = true and supplies no wrapper,
so configure cannot get past this check.

The check already treats execution as optional when cross compiling - the
branch below it warns rather than errors, precisely because the program cannot
be run - but that branch is never reached, because the raise happens while the
result is being produced. So ask for only the half of the question that can be
answered here: that a minimal SpiderMonkey program compiles and links against
the SpiderMonkey being built. The warning about verifying startup on the
target still applies and is still printed.

Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -255,20 +255,37 @@
 # Check if a minimal SpiderMonkey program compiles, links, and runs. If not,
 # it's most likely the case that SpiderMonkey was configured incorrectly, for
 # example by building mozglue as a shared library.
-minimal_program = cxx.run('''
+minimal_program_code = '''
 #include <js/Initialization.h>
 int main(void) {
     if (!JS_Init()) return 1;
     JS_ShutDown();
     return 0;
 }
-''',
-    args: debug_arg, dependencies: spidermonkey,
-    name: 'SpiderMonkey sanity check')
+'''
 
 recommended_configuration = ''' Check the recommended configuration:
 https://github.com/spidermonkey-embedders/spidermonkey-embedding-examples/blob/esr91/docs/Building%20SpiderMonkey.md'''
-if not minimal_program.compiled()
+
+if meson.is_cross_build()
+    # cxx.run() raises "Can not run test applications in this cross
+    # environment" unless the cross file supplies an exe_wrapper, and it does
+    # so before any of the branches below get a chance to look at the result.
+    # The execution half of this check is already declared optional when cross
+    # compiling, so ask only for the half that can be answered here.
+    minimal_program_compiled = cxx.links(minimal_program_code,
+        args: debug_arg, dependencies: spidermonkey,
+        name: 'SpiderMonkey sanity check')
+    minimal_program_returncode = 0
+else
+    minimal_program = cxx.run(minimal_program_code,
+        args: debug_arg, dependencies: spidermonkey,
+        name: 'SpiderMonkey sanity check')
+    minimal_program_compiled = minimal_program.compiled()
+    minimal_program_returncode = minimal_program.returncode()
+endif
+
+if not minimal_program_compiled
     error('''A minimal SpiderMonkey program
 could not be compiled or linked. Most likely you should build it with a
 different configuration.''' + recommended_configuration)
@@ -277,7 +294,7 @@
 SpiderMonkey program executes will not be performed. Before shipping GJS, you
 should check that it does not crash on startup, since building SpiderMonkey with
 the wrong configuration may cause that.''' + recommended_configuration)
-elif minimal_program.returncode() != 0
+elif minimal_program_returncode != 0
     error('''A minimal SpiderMonkey program
 failed to execute. Most likely you should build it with a different
 configuration.''' + recommended_configuration)
